# Context

## Background
Candidate run 45709812198 for v0.8.0 failed on macos-15-intel in
make check: TestLargeFileUploadsInBoundedBatches stopped at 11.28 s
with "hubsync: read frame: read tcp ...: i/o timeout". The rerun of
that job passed, and v0.8.0 was cut from 915df53. This fix came after
the tag, because it changes a test only.

## Why This Way
The subject of the test is the batch bound, not a timeout. Its
budget was the fixture default of 10 s for one request. The
production default is 60 s. The test now names the production value
and allows two round trips, one for each batch.

## Gotchas
- A first throwaway proxy delayed replies after 32 MiB from the
  client. It delayed nothing: the test hub takes compressed batches,
  and a batch of one repeated letter is a few KB on the wire. The
  trigger that works is the zstd frame signature.
- The budget of 60 s was not measured against a real slow hub.
- make check with GOFLAGS=-count=1 passed on this tree.
